// ============================================================
// COLD OPEN — Side A
// ============================================================
=== cold_open ===
@ctx Pitch dark. A cassette recorded in 1982 is playing: a teenage girl whispering into a tape recorder on a strange night. Parts are lost to hiss.
@amb static
@wait 1
@sfx tape_insert
@wait 0.6
@cg cg_tape side_a
@fx clear
@wait 1.2
@sfx tape_play
@wait 1
TAPE(girl): —kay. Okay, it's going. The little wheels are turning.
TAPE(girl): This is J—— *hiss* ——, and it's eight fifty-two p.m., Saturday, October ninth, nineteen eighty-two.
TAPE(girl): Every light on Corson Street just went out. All at once. Not a power cut — the Novaks' TV is still on, I can see it flickering through their curtains. They turned off the lamps. Everybody did. At the exact same second.
TAPE(girl): Like somebody rang a bell only grown-ups can hear.
TAPE(girl): Mom went to bed at eight. Dad went to bed at eight. Dad has never gone to bed at eight in his life. He watches Carson. He *likes* Carson.
TAPE(girl): Mémère told me once: on Quiet night, ma belle, you stay in your bed and you don't look out the window.
TAPE(girl): So. Obviously.
@sfx static_burst
@fx glitch
TAPE(girl): There's a light. Way past the end of the street, up on the hill. Green. Like a lantern.
TAPE(girl): It isn't moving. Everything else is. Everything else is getting *farther away.* That doesn't make sense. I'm saying it out loud so it's on the tape. It doesn't make any sense.
@wait 2
TAPE(girl): ...
TAPE(girl): ——ssie?
TAPE(girl): What are you doing out there? You're supposed to be in bed — hey. Hey! Stay there. Stay right there, I'm coming down—
@sfx footsteps
@sfx door_open
@sfx wind_gust
@wait 2.5
The tape runs on for eleven more minutes.
Wind. A screen door banging in the wind, over and over.
Nobody comes back to turn it off.
@sfx tape_stop
@amb stop
@cg off
@fx blackout
@wait 2
-> ch1
